Package: lunarcast
Type: Package
Title: Calendar Variation Models for Time Series with Moving Holidays
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Novri", "Suhermi", email = "novri.suhermi@its.ac.id",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Forecasts monthly and quarterly time series affected by moving
    holidays whose Gregorian dates change every year, such as Eid al-Fitr,
    Eid al-Adha, the Chinese New Year and Easter. Holiday effects enter
    through window regressors, may differ between occurrences (a two-level
    model in which the effect of the next occurrence is forecast from past
    effects) and are combined with a regression with ARIMA errors whose
    trend and seasonal structure is chosen by calendar-aware
    cross-validation. The classical calendar variation model, with a dummy
    for the holiday month and a constant effect, is included for
    comparison, together with tools for rolling-origin evaluation.
